SUMMARY:2770 - Sourdough 101
DESCRIPTION:Join instructor Loretta Beiler for a warm and welcoming introduction to the art of sourdough baking. In this beginner-friendly workshop\, you will learn how to create and care for your own sourdough starter\, master the steps to make two beautiful loaves from start to finish\, and taste freshly baked sourdough served with butter and seasonal jams. Loretta’s approachable teaching style and passion for baking will leave you inspired and ready to bring the joy of sourdough into your own kitchen. You will also head home with a starter kit and all the essentials you need to continue baking. \nDemonstration Class. BYOB. Ages 16 and up. \n\nHow to create and maintain your own sourdough starter\nStep-by-step process to make two sourdough loaves\nTasting of sourdough with delicious butter and jams and whipped feta with honey \nTake-home kit with an active starter and baking essentials
URL:https://zestchef.com/class/2770-sourdough-101/
LOCATION:Zest Cooking School\, 1180 Erbs Quarry Road\, Lititz\, PA\, 17543\, United States
CATEGORIES:Basics and Techniques,Healthy Eating,Let's Bake,Masterclass
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://zestchef.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/sourdough-101-scaled-e1743620961517.jpg
END:VEVENT
